.SH NAME
bashpass - local command-line password manager written in Bash

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bashpass
[\fIOPTION\fR] [\fINAME\fR]
.br
.B bashpass
.B -G
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGUMENT\fR ...]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B BashPass
is a command-line password manager written in Bash.
Together with
.BR gpg (1),
it stores passwords locally.

Passwords are encrypted using the user's GnuPG key before being stored in
the password store. BashPass does not require a remote service to store
passwords.

The password store can optionally be managed as a Git repository using the
.BR -G
option.

Password names may contain letters, numbers, underscores, periods, @, plus
signs, and hyphens.

.SH COMMANDS

.TP
.BR -a ", " --add " [" NAME ]
Add a password. The password can either be entered manually or generated
automatically. If \fINAME\fR is omitted, BashPass prompts for one.

.TP
.BR -c ", " --copy " [" NAME ]
Copy a password to the clipboard. The clipboard is cleared after the
configured timeout. If \fINAME\fR is omitted, BashPass prompts for one.

.TP
.BR -d ", " --delete " [" NAME ]
Delete a password without asking for confirmation. If \fINAME\fR is omitted,
BashPass prompts for one.

.TP
.BR -l ", " --list
List all passwords in the password store.

.TP
.BR -s ", " --show " [" NAME ]
Print a password to standard output. If \fINAME\fR is omitted, BashPass
prompts for one.

.TP
.BR -u ", " --update " [" NAME ]
Update an existing password. The password can either be entered manually or
generated automatically. If \fINAME\fR is omitted, BashPass prompts for one.

.TP
.BR -G ", " --git " COMMAND " [" ARGUMENT ...]
Run a Git command with the password store as its working directory. Arguments
are passed directly to Git.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show a brief help message.

.TP
.BR -v ", " --version
Show the BashPass version.

.SH ENVIRONMENT

BashPass is configured using environment variables. Settings not explicitly
configured use their default values.

.TP
.B BASHPASS_KEY_ID
GnuPG key ID used to encrypt passwords. If unset, BashPass prompts for a key
ID when it starts. The value may be the last 8 characters or the complete
40-character GnuPG fingerprint.

.TP
.B BASHPASS_PASSWD_LENGTH
Default length of generated passwords. The default is 14 characters. This
value can be overridden when adding or updating a password.

.TP
.B BASHPASS_PASSWD_STORE
Location of the password store. The default is
.IR ~/.local/share/bashpass .

.TP
.B BASHPASS_CLIPBOARD_COPY_CMD
Command used to copy a password to the clipboard. The default is
.BR "wl-copy" .

.TP
.B BASHPASS_CLIPBOARD_CLEAR_CMD
Command used to clear the clipboard. The default is
.BR "wl-copy --clear" .

.TP
.B BASHPASS_CLIPBOARD_TIMER
Number of seconds a copied password remains in the clipboard. The default is
10 seconds.

.SH EXAMPLES

.TP
.B bashpass -a github
Add a password named
.IR github .

.TP
.B bashpass -c github
Copy the
.I github
password to the clipboard.

.TP
.B bashpass -d github
Delete the
.I github
password without asking for confirmation.

.TP
.B API_KEY="$(bashpass -s api-key)"
Use a password directly in a shell variable.

.TP
.B bashpass -G init
Initialize the password store as a Git repository.

.TP
.B bashpass -G add -A
Stage all changes in the password store.

.TP
.B bashpass -G commit -m "Update passwords"
Commit changes using Git.

.TP
.B bashpass -G push
Push the password store to its configured remote.

.SH FILES

.TP
.I ~/.local/share/bashpass/
Default password store.

